","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.7.dev4.official [755fa449c], v4.7.dev3.official [60fff00a6]\n- Not reproducible in v4.7.dev2.official [778cf54da], v4.6.2.stable.official [71f334935]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev4 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8157) - AMD Ryzen 5 7600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 31.75 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the editor is in a transform mode and a 3D-pickable node is currently selected, left-clicking any of its pickable parts seems to start the mouse drag movement with a message such as \"Translating: (x,y,z)\".\n\nNo undo history for that movement is recorded, so using undo will reverse other previous changes instead and leaves the node misplaced. \n\nLeft clicking again will continue \"dragging\" the node if still overlapping a pickable part.  \nLeft-clicking can break out of the drag if the mouse is over something else (transform gizmo, other node, background).\nRight-clicking or pressing esc cancels the movement with \"Transform Aborted\".\n\nThe drag movement can be activated by 3d-picking the node while in any of the modes Transform, Move, Rotate or Scale, but node position seems to only change once in Transform or Move modes. (Eg you can pick the node in rotate mode and the node will start moving after you switch to transform or move mode)\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add a MeshInstance3D with default BoxMesh to the scene\n2. Put the editor scene view in transform mode (Q key by default)\n3. Select the mesh node by clicking it on the scene view or hierarchy\n4. Left-click the mesh in the scene view in a position that doesn't overlap transform gizmos\n5. Move your mouse to see the node being dragged around\n6. End the drag by clicking somewhere where the transform gizmos overlap your cursor.\n7. Try the editor undo & redo (ctrl+z and ctrl+shift+z) to see the node movement wasn't recorded in the undo history \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118603/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118603/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}